{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1121378-let-s-brainstorm-cooking-a-chronicle-w-xiongrey","id":1121378,"title":"Let's Brainstorm: Cooking a Chronicle w/ xiongrey","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-07-27T10:34:33-07:00","id":1121378,"title":"Let's Brainstorm: Cooking a Chronicle w/ xiongrey","content":"Sorry for the cheesy title ^.^;<br /> <br /> So i'm creating a chronicle for my fianc\u00e9, My brother, and his wife. None of them frequent these forums and are not likely to so I feel pretty safe posting this. <br /> <br /> I'm brainstorming some ideas for the Chronicle and I feel like it would benefit from other people piping in ideas if they so chose so I'm posting on the forums. If no one posts, that is ok, I will continue to brainstorm this until it's all hammered out. <br /> <br /> <b>So what is the game about?:</b> <br /> In very Broad strokes, It's an overarching story that starts with innocents of the neighborhood kids and their brush with the supernatural and moves onto a campy &quot;horror camping trip&quot; story that ends with the story moving into one of several game lines: V:tR, W:tF, M:tA, P:tC, C:tL, G:tS, D:tD, B:tP (notably absent are the lines that will not likely see a 2nd Ed by the time the second Story is concluded (so in the next year and a half. Also absent is Hunter because my sister-in-law does not seem to want to play Hunter.)<br /> <br /> The players do not and will not know at the time that I'm working towards one of the game lines and by the time they find out, it shouldn't look as if it was going anywhere else. How will I choose which to really pursue? Well I'll watch the players and the characters and see what they're enjoying about and through out the first story (if they're really enjoying RPing the fear and the running than that's a hint they might enjoy C:tL w/ these characters, but if they choose to fix things with a passion then that's a hint they might enjoy a W:tF game. And if they try to use circumstances to better benefit their characters in someway than that's a pretty clear analogue to V:tR. These are just examples, it'll be subjective.). Secondly, the first act of the second story (them in the woods) will introduce quite a few plot hooks/foreshadowings/Chekhov's guns. These are analogous to a play style or modus operandi of a game line. Following one or taking much interest in one chooses how the rest of the story goes (imagine Cabin in the Woods and how the &quot;horror&quot; was chosen a third of the way into the movie).<br /> <br /> Examples of this would be: if the characters immediately go to the power station higher in the mountain, their need to fix things first and foremost would indicate a W:tF plot (werewolves like to fix things more spiritual but it would be good). If they immediately attempt to follow the random symbols on a few of the trees near the campsite, convinced that they must mean something and start following the clues then the story gets colored w/ M:tA tones. If they explore a little more despite the warning than it becomes a C:tL game. You get the idea.<br /> <br /> The chosen direction will color the weird things that happened in Act 1 and it will be a fairly straightforward campy horror story from there on with it ending in whichever story line. <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#006400\">tl:dr: First story is an Innocents game a la Stranger Things/Super 8/Goonies/ect. Second story is <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/Camp\" target=\"_blank\">campy</a> college kids <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/DontGoInTheWoods\" target=\"_blank\">horror in the woods</a> story w/ diverging pathways each ending in one of eight game lines.</span><br /> <br /> <b>The Process:</b><br /> Trust me, this is less ambitious than it sounds. I originally started this out with it becoming a C:tL game solely and mostly fleshed what that would look like out but then got to thinking that I could do the first two stories and have them end in almost any Game Line that could want. So here we are. A lot of this is going to be subjective to the players. So the main three things I need to do are:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Identify, in broad strokes, what about each of the eight game lines the players would enjoy (or players in general) and then seed that into the stories.</li> <li>Provide foreshadowings appropriate to each theme that clearly attract the players in that direction if that's the kind of direction they like playing with.</li> <li>Fit the trappings of the chosen Game Line into the plot and feel of the Second Story so that each choices addresses at least some of the foreshadowings.</li> </ol><br /> ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~<br /> <br /> So with that out of the way, here's my musings attempting to approach each of these three (sorry if they're a bit rambly, I get rambly when brainstorming)<br /> <br /> <b>1. What appeals to players about each of the eight Game Lines?</b><ul><li>Vampire: Visceral Drama and Personal Horror<ul><li>What makes someone want to play a vampire?<ul><li>They want the politics.</li> </ul></li> </ul></li> <li>Werewolf: Phantom threats and Savage Fury<ul><li>What makes someone want to play WtF?<ul><li>They Want to hunt.</li> <li>They want to fix things that ought to be fixed.</li> <li>The feel close to their surroundings.</li> </ul></li> </ul></li> <li>Mage: awe inspiring truths and deadly hubris<ul><li>What makes someone want to play MtA<ul><li>The powers</li> <li>The searching for clues.</li> <li>Special Mention: J likes Mage only when it is similar to Constantine (the Show)... So Adamantine Arrow.</li> </ul></li> </ul></li> <li>Promethean: Human Lives, both new and stolen<ul><li>What makes someone want to play PtC?<ul><li>The journey</li> <li>Playing something not human</li> <li>Trying new things</li> <li>The connection of change</li> </ul></li> </ul></li> <li>Changeling: Desperate escape and beautiful madness<ul><li>What makes someone want to play CtL?<ul><li>The madness</li> <li>The weirdness</li> <li>The pledges and contracts</li> <li>The fear</li> </ul></li> </ul></li> <li>Geist: Second chances and Last Rights<ul><li>What makes someone want to play Geist?<ul><li>The party</li> <li>Interacting with the dead</li> <li>The tons and tons of artefacts</li> <li>The dichotomy of basically being possessed</li> <li>The cool group cults that players form.</li> </ul></li> </ul></li> <li>Demon: The Fall\u2026 And the Rise<ul><li>What makes someone want to play DtD?<ul><li>Knowing the underlying foundation of reality and hiding from it.</li> <li>The transforming into a weird creature</li> <li>Being completely alien.</li> <li>Outsmarting cosmic computer processes</li> <li>Essentially feeling like a deity trapped in the mortal realm</li> </ul></li> </ul></li> <li>Beast: Strange hungers and living nightmares<ul><li>What makes someone want to play BtP?<ul><li>Crossovery</li> <li>Interaction w/ personal heroes</li> <li>Attempting to balance the Hungers</li> <li>crossovery</li> </ul></li> </ul></li> </ul><br /> <b>2. What would the second story look like for each? (while keeping the campy horror in the woods feel for at least 2 out of 3 acts)</b><ul><li>Vampire: Caves<ul><li>The characters check down at the caves. (<span style=\"color:#006400\">Why??)</span> There is a hive of vampires down there, mostly Mekhet and Nosferatu. They have to survive the feral monsters a la 30 days of night style. They find out a little on what's happening on their need for survival and the attempting to beat out the horde of evil creatures. Near the end, not all of the monsters are insane and after them which would give hints to future story hooks and provide reason for the end result of them being imbraced and a way for them (and their Sires) to reenter the City.</li> </ul></li> <li>Werewolf: The Power Station<ul><li>The characters check the Power station to attempt to fix the outage that occurred at a critical time. <span style=\"color:#006400\">(If they're camping... how would this effect them at all?? Maybe they're in a cabin just like Until Dawn, though I hoped to avoid too many comparisons).</span> Weird things occur there. Unbeknownst to the Characters, the local Spirits are going crazy and the reason for this is a plot by a Bale Hound(s?) That brought the neighboring (-ish) Pure Pack and a couple Forsaken Packs into proximity all during the time that one of the group is about to go through their First Change (all the chars would be WWs but I didn't want to force them to be the same Auspice). Most of the story would not be overtly Werewolf and would focus on them being hunted by Spirits dicking with them and other more malicious Werewolves before they put the clues together and the First change happens in the third act leading to the full third act w/ a few of the Forsaken packs and the &quot;pups&quot; given a job (prolly back at the Power Station to be poetic).</li> </ul></li> <li>Mage: Tree Tags... wait no... perhaps they are at a lodge... so: Map Symbol<ul><li>I'm really unsure of this one. There needs to be some sort of monster that explains the earlier attacks that push the campy horror in act one that continues through Act 2. But there also needs to be clues that the characters follow. Following clues to get to the bottom of arcane things going on is like the classic example of Mages Awakening. It also needs to provide hints of the future plot hooks. It also needs to provide me w/ an easy way to narrate the timeskip between the end of the story (aka the awakening) and the beginning of the next (they're in a Cabal, they have pledged themselves to any one of the Orders, they understand at least the basics of Mage society, ETC). to do this I'd think I'd need at least a mage to be there. hmmmm... how about this.</li> <li>The characters, amidst the attack (or whatever it is) and the power outage decide to look into the arcane yet somehow significant seeming symbol on [a map? some other piece of paper? the wall of the...cabin? the wall of the tent?]. What follows is clue after clue with some sort of abyssal something that seems to constantly get in the way of learning more. What's more, there is this gruff woodsman (a thyrsus looking into an atlantean temple for the Mysterium...but they don't know that) that dismisses the characters, tells them to be wary and stop nosing into things they wont understand. In the end the characters continue, halfway outsmart the... essence? (got to figure out what it is later) and find the temple. At this point they've been taunted with learning this &quot;terrible truth&quot; that causes others to go insane and they've been blocked from knowing it and at this point they should feel so taunted that they enter despite the dangers at the last third of the story. Mostly with Thyrsus attempting to keep them safe, entering into this at the end of their journey, they awaken and write their names on a watch tower (well their souls do anyway) and the story ends (with the Thyrsus bringing them to the concilium in the Time Skip and them being given over to any of the Orders and forming a Cabal legal in the consilium's regard. (all during the time skip allowed for the Mage Char-gen).</li> </ul></li> <li>Changeling: Tree Tags (I like this for Changeling better)<ul><li>The characters find Tags with different numbers as they approach their cabin/campsite. near the end of the first act after the attack (however that goes down) the characters decide to follow the tags to safety (they might have been told, when asking a guide, that the tags were put up so that campers or anyone else can easily find their way out). Well after the attack, the characters decide to follow the numbers on the Trod (wink). the path seems a little weirder than the remember and they keep cutting their ankles on the underbrush. Most of the story really revolves around attempting to find safety at a place that is owned by a Hobgoblin and then trying to escape (a la the ginger bread house or something of the like but it needs to be a lot more inviting to modern college kids who just ran from something they don't really know... I'll have to think about that). Anyway the second act is all finding that place and at the end getting stuck under threat from the hobgoblin. the third act is the harrowing attempt to escape and getting the end of what they thought was the path and it turns out to be Faerie with some dramatic last words being said by the Title they meet on arrival(/capture).</li> <li>Really there is so many things in the Hedge that I could use for the whole story... Might have to think of something else that fits wth the Campy in the woods horror theme. More thinking is required. the end result is the same though.</li> <li><span style=\"color:#006400\">I might still like this one the best. So I might still just do this but we'll see.</span></li> </ul></li> <li>Geist: ?... The Cabin in the Woods<ul><li>This one is a big If because I don't know if Geist will get it's 2nd Edition by then. If it doesn't seem close by the time the second story is about to be run, then the plot hooks I create for it will be thrown out.</li> <li>I imagine getting a hook in there where death is important. Like maybe a haunted mansion that might be close or a graveyard... or something. That one will be hard.</li> <li>will think on that one later.</li> <li>ok back after a nights rest. Lets try this (going to just write and see what I come up with):<ul><li>The characters explore the cabin (still not sure if they're gonna start in a cabin yet but let's go with it). After all there must be answers hidden within the place, the players and their characters are genre saavy enough to know some secret is baried within even if nothing has yet pointed to it. (ie they make up their own cause similar to how Sin-eaters make any ritual they read off some wiki actually work... the experimentation and hoakyness seems pretty anoalogous). From then on it becomes a fairly typical haunted house story with the big reveal that most of the ghosts they find and get scared or hurt from throughout Act 2 arn't actually bad and are also terrorized by the death thing (not a geist, some powerful ghost would work tho, maybe working for a death lord setting up hooks for future stories). The end result is the death or near death of the characters but of their own volition (typically anyway, I'll have to figure that one out...) with the last scene being me narrating a shadow in the dark saying something ominous like &quot;it's not the dieing you should be worrying about but the life unlived&quot; and then a hand reaching out to them. At which point they'd add on the Bound template and I'd narrate the time-skip.</li> </ul></li> </ul></li> <li>Demon: The Radio Tower<ul><li>So D:tD and P:tC are both game lines where the players would essentially be creating new characters. On the plus side of that, two full stories is an ok amount of time to have with a mortal character, but I'd have to watch the player's carefully to see if they would even want to do that (without asking them and, you know, ruin the surprise).</li> <li>The characters get hints that they might not be alone (obviously from the attack at the end of Act 1) but further more that there might be some sort of intelligent plan behind what is happening. The characters know that the mountain itself has a long history in the area mostly around the Radio Tower at the top of the mountain. The characters decide to climb the mountain, haunted by the things after them, to get through to someone out side of the mountain. The 2nd act consists of the characters going from place to place as they move up the mountain, dodging attacks from creatures, finding a group of three survivors who're hiding out in the woods and haven't been able to get out. All the while they start to see weirdness in the forest, some trees seem to have wiring under the bark, the ground is producing an abnormal amount of static electricity, and the creatures that come at night have this hollow sound to them as if they were recorded. The 3rd and climactic act is the finding of the tower and finding out that there is a cult within apparently worshiping the wires. The characters attempt to get to the inside with the three survivors (a Ring of demons who're trying to take down this Infrastructure) and find out the Truth of this all. In the final bit, the strangers offer them to make a pact that &quot;only one of them can make it out of this alive&quot; so the survivors will distract the cultists long enough for the characters to breach the Infrastructure and stop it from getting its signal out (that's been causing cryptids to go nuts). I'll have to word it Differently but essentially they trick them into a soul pact in the most harrowing circumstances. Getting inside they find out that the truth was that the signal was being broadcast to some all-powerful machine god who intended to use their essence as oil for the machine. They destroy the unit after losing some health on some of the weirdness and the game closes as the 3 Demons (who went loud to take care of the cultists en masse off screen come to take their debt.</li> </ul></li> <li>Promethean: The Lab<ul><li>So D:tD and P:tC are both game lines where the players would essentially be creating new characters. On the plus side of that, two full stories is an ok amount of time to have with a mortal character, but I'd have to watch the player's carefully to see if they would even want to do that (without asking them and, you know, ruin the surprise).</li> <li>This one is going to be hard... It needs to hit on the idea of Alchemy and Science (since that's a mindset the players will need if they go this route...) and it also needs to touch on the despair of what it means to be a Promethean before the end of the story yet it still needs to be up on the campy teen horror movie feel. hmmm, idea...:</li> <li>The characters find a lab in the Cabin in Act 1 and think nothing of it at first. However something about the attack at the end of Act 1 (strewn body parts or something? For the most part it sounds like they came with at least one person who obviously dies at the end of Act 1 to kick start the plot). The characters visit the the Lab and read some of the alchemical journals there. there's a lot of paper that's been pulled off and it's obvious that there's been someone in here since they last saw the lab. upon further inspection they learn that there's a medical facility by the old mines.The characters are harrowed through out the house (by pandorans who really just want the Prometheans). All the while they get this gut wrenching feeling about the creatures that seem to want to harvest them or eat them. Al together it should give off a The Hills Have Eyes vibe. In the end, (near the end of Act 2 and start of act 3) they decide to go on the proactive and kill the things at the clinic, they've got the weapons and the know-how. Act 3 ends with the characters finding the clinic, successfully attacking the unwitting Prometheans while they were (somewhat innocently) attempting to procreate, the battle leaves all 3 parties dead (since Pandorans were involved) right as they were successful in the creation of the new Prometheans. The story ends with their dying eyes seeing the new born prometheans gaze on at them with curious and confused eyes.</li> </ul></li> <li>Beast: The Mine? (idk, just thought of it)<ul><li>I have not read Beast, Like at all but I want a reason to. So for the moment I have no idea.</li> </ul></li> <li>Deviant: ?<ul><li>Deviant isn't out yet but it might be by the time this story comes around. I imagine something to do with a cult or corporation doing hidden activities in the mountains and the characters attempt to find out the weirdness of the things going on and get off the mountain alive, take down one of the facilities on the mountain and then get captured at the base of the mountain a la the end of the First Resident Evil movie. It strikes me as similar to Deviant themes (that we know so far) to rebel against the attackers. Kinda like Demons but much more head on so Rushing into it could be similar to the Deviant path.</li> </ul></li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-27T11:05:46-07:00","id":1121401,"title":"","content":"So, for Demon, you could have the characters become Stigmatic, or revealed as Demon-blooded (likely Latents). If they must go full splat, you could even leverage the above and give them Sympathetic Demon, then slowly transition in them playing their Sympathetic Demon. Or check out the Homebrew merit thread for options.<br /> <br /> For Promethean, they could go Alchemist. Again, if they must go full splat, you could have them killed or transformed, and their Ghost/new state be a Promethean's ally, maybe even merging with the Created eventually.<br /> <br /> EDIT: for Promethean camp, the Created could even be the PCs' own bodies, and the PC linger as brains-in-jars!<br /> <br /> For Beast, have them stalked and terrorized by an old Beast (or a Brood or them). Either it was because the Beast(s) we're trying to awaken/Devour the PCs into realizing they were Beasts all alone, or to pass on their own Horrors to the PCs. Either way, the PCs would then be Beasts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 07-27-2017, 02:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-27T13:58:39-07:00","id":1121515,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1121378-let-s-brainstorm-cooking-a-chronicle-w-xiongrey?p=1121401#post1121401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, for Demon, you could have the characters become Stigmatic, or revealed as Demon-blooded (likely Latents). If they must go full splat, you could even leverage the above and give them Sympathetic Demon, then slowly transition in them playing their Sympathetic Demon. Or check out the Homebrew merit thread for options.<br /> <br /> For Promethean, they could go Alchemist. Again, if they must go full splat, you could have them killed or transformed, and their Ghost/new state be a Promethean's ally, maybe even merging with the Created eventually.<br /> <br /> EDIT: for Promethean camp, the Created could even be the PCs' own bodies, and the PC linger as brains-in-jars!<br /> <br /> For Beast, have them stalked and terrorized by an old Beast (or a Brood or them). Either it was because the Beast(s) we're trying to awaken/Devour the PCs into realizing they were Beasts all alone, or to pass on their own Horrors to the PCs. Either way, the PCs would then be Beasts.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really like the Brain in Jars Option! <br /> <br /> I suppose its not imperative that they go full splat. So I started out with just changeling and created a story-to-story flow like this:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Innocents --&gt; Teens horror getting lost in the woods --&gt; Escaping Faerieland (and learning all the bargains and the things they need to remember as a part of playing C:tL) --&gt; either Dealing w/ fetches or a time-skip to them already in their courts --&gt; dealing w/ actions made in Story 2/3 as a new changeling comes through which leads to their keeper finding them easier. --&gt; Story about the great hunt on their characters --&gt; an interim story on the Goblin Markets that ends w/ them finding out something important on how their Keeper works --&gt; Story on outwitting the Huntsman that's been after them that ends w/ them just outside arcadia and a hint on how actually to defeat their Keeper's title --&gt; climactic story which either ends w/ them defeating the Fae for now and leaving or they take the Titles becoming True Fae themselves, or they decide to take down the Wyrd itself (which starts another whole chronicle about finding the literal plot hooks and plot holes in the entire narrative and slowly breaking and unweaving them).</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> So I had just thought about taking that formula and applying it to the differrent splats that I could be working with. However, it is tottally possible for a Demon story to be had with Demon-blooded PCs! I do like that idea as it also has the slow story to story progression w/ timeskips that I had intended! <br /> <br /> so yes, I love that Idea and will likely do that!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-08T17:52:04-07:00","id":1138759,"title":"","content":"Alright, well with the deadline looming near, I need to create the first Story. The innocents game. The one I want to have a feel like a cross between The Goonies, Stranger Things, and Gothika. <br /> <br /> I'm not intending this to be a full on horror story nor do I want to beat the horror into the characters. At the same time, it needs to have horror elements but ultimately end up on a note like the Goonies. I want it to be confusing like Stranger Things and Gothika at first till things are found out. What I'm taking from Gothika is the Plot structure where two things are happening to the characters that are actually related. How that relates to Gothika... prolly should put that in spoilers...<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> The two things that are happening are:<br /> 1. The character is being haunted by an angry and vengeful ghost.<br /> 2. Something corrupt and sinister is happening around the facility that the character works.<br /> <br /> The plot structure I like is how the investigation into the former informs the latter. I couldn't find a trope to that effect but that, I want that. </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> So Plenty of Chekov's items. <br /> <br /> Now before I dive into it, I can't fully create it till the characters are made and I see their aspirations and I see how the players are making their characters and get a feel for what they are going to find fun. I know that I want it to have horror elements but it shouldn't feel like a typical CofD horror (that's supposed to build overtime for this specific Chron)<br /> <br /> <b>Antagonist(s)</b><br /> <br /> It could be a ghost. That would be like Gothica... I'm begging to think that I should dive right into the Faerie Hints rather than a split focus but make it vague enough that I can rework if I can tell that the players don't want to go that route. I was thinking this because I thought some changeling drama or something might be the overall issue that occurs over the course of the story. <br /> <br /> So all these events or antagonists need to really be the hint dropper to the real villain/event (as was the case with Gothika).<br /> <br /> Ghost<br /> Fae<br /> Science<br /> Spirits<br /> Infrastructure<br /> Magic<br /> Other creature<br /> A vampire<br /> Beasts<br /> <br /> There\u2019s others but these are coming to mind most currently. The main thing I need to think of is:<ul><li>How can I introduce these threatening phenomena in a way that only the children characters (and not the adults or police or something) would be affected by and be able to see/find?</li> <li>How can that conflict and threat inform and lead back to a more subtle but much more relevant and deadly threat?</li> <li>What would the accompanying real threat be?</li> </ul><br /> I\u2019ll need to think on this.<br /> <br /> <br /> \u200b<b>Structure:</b> (all 4 acts have a beginning, middle, and an end)<ul><li>Act 1: Hints/introductions/checkov\u2019s items<ul><li>Beginning:</li> <li>Middle:</li> <li>End: </li> </ul></li> <li>Act 2: Issues happen to the characters. Both the real issue that is subtle and the issue that pushes them more immediately.<ul><li>Beginning:</li> <li>Middle:</li> <li>End: </li> </ul></li> <li>Act 3: The situations worsen but with clear clues that can be followed through with choices. This must be an act of the characters, this is the beginning of the loss of innocence as they endeavor to beat whatever ails them.<ul><li>Beginning:</li> <li>Middle:</li> <li>End: </li> </ul></li> <li>Act 4: The characters have all the knowledge they need and the path is clear but the stakes are up (time limit?)<ul><li>Beginning:</li> <li>Middle:</li> <li>End:</li> </ul></li> </ul><br /> <br /> We\u2019re doing character creation tomorrow so once I have more information on their characters and what they are looking for as players I\u2019ll be able to do a bit more but for now there\u2019s so many options that I can\u2019t really deal with at the moment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-09T08:28:17-07:00","id":1138897,"title":"","content":"Well, to hint the monster/antagonist towards fae, but still leave it ambiguous, structure information about it in the form of a rhyme, fairy tale, or folklore. Those lend themselves to fae things easily, but can still refer to other things.<br /> <br /> For why only kids are effective: maybe the antagonist can only be seen by non-adults, or adults prevent it from manifesting. Or it only targets kids alone. Or maybe the adults are dealing with another, more obvious crisis right now, leaving the kids to pursue the more subtle mystery.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-11T11:23:35-07:00","id":1139493,"title":"","content":"Wow so the CC session was amazing and I\u2019ve got a lot to go on now! In addition to creating their characters, I opened up Mr. Gone\u2019s Innocent\u2019s Neighborhood and Small-Town worksheets to their own creation with me as the scribe. It, went, <i>fantastically!</i> So before I reply to you <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7212_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7212\" data-vbnamecard=\"7212\">Vent0</a> , because that is a fantastic idea, I\u2019m going to just list out the results from the CC session Starting with the family unit that the PCs belong to then move on to the Neighborhood then to the city as a whole.<br /> <br /> Again, my interjected thoughts are in green.<br /> <br /> As a side note, I came up with a Chronicle name for the Chronicle. The reasoning for it will become obvious below but it is called \u201c<b>The Dead End\u201d</b>.<br /> <br /> ~~~~~<br /> <br /> So without further ado: <b>The Branson Foghorn family. </b><br /> <br /> Derek and Delilah Branson both grew up, met, married, and had a kid all without ever leaving the town of Suburbia. The pair both worked at the factory back in town and they both were not great parents to their only child Sean Branson preferring the company of a beer and their friends that lived next door.<br /> <br /> Two years ago, Delilah died in an accident which only worsened Derek\u2019s negligent, drinking, and abusive behavior. This behavior was only slightly tempered by meeting and eventually marrying Gizelah Foghorn (now Branson). Giselah not only brought with her an oppressive controlling temperament (akin to the evil step mother) but also her own children to an unnamed previous father named Josh and Ingrid Foghorn (whose last names did not change after the marriage).<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\">[imo, their family is a whole lot darker than I had intended the whole story to be because I wasn\u2019t sure what they would want to explore. So I was originally going for a Goonies adventure slight-thriller vibe. However, I am pleased that they seem to want more than the superficial explorations into different themes of humanity.]</span><br /> <br /> The player characters are Sean Branson (11) Played by my brother, Josh Foghorn (11) played by my fianc\u00e9, and Ingrid Foghorn (8) played by my sister-in-law.<br /> <br /> Sean is the generous but aloof cool punk kid styled after John Conner from The Terminator 2 with a similar appearance of dark brown kept hair and green eyes. He is well liked and likes most others in turn but due to his home life, attempts to spend most of his time away in back alleys while his dad drinks. Other activities include breaking and entering places to hide out in. His aspirations include: (as a note, I allowed a fourth very long-term player aspiration if they wanted)<ul><li>Run away from home.</li> <li>Break his father and step-mother up.</li> <li>Make a hidden \u201chome\u201d on the streets</li> <li>Create their own faction and take over the town.</li> </ul>Josh coped with being the eldest son in a mentally abusive family was to shut down but lash out in silent ways. Josh is the determined and greedy bored kleptomaniac kid, sneaking around because he can. While he\u2019s not super fond of people, to most of his peers he seems aloof and contemptuous. He doesn\u2019t steal because he desires the items per say rather he just wants to steal just cause. It\u2019s his way of breaking out of his chains. His aspirations include:<ul><li>Skip a class</li> <li>Eat for free</li> <li>Rob a store</li> </ul><span style=\"color:#008000\">[note: it looks like they\u2019d enjoy a story set during the school year]</span><br /> <br /> Josh\u2019s younger sister Ingrid though, by contrast became the perfectionist. Though she is younger, she became the loyal smart outcast of her family who coped with her family by telling those around whatever they wanted to hear whether it was the truth or not (and it often wasn\u2019t). Even still she strives to be the best she can be in other people\u2019s eyes, feeling like she needs to prove herself all the more. She is very dedicated to her schoolwork for a Third Grader and has a knack for it with a great memory. Her aspirations include:<ul><li>Be a <u>real</u> part of her brother\u2019s friend group <span style=\"color:#008000\">[note, so she wants to explore that challenge]</span></li> <li>Be the best in her class.</li> <li>Run away from home.</li> <li>Be in charge of the factories of the town.</li> </ul>Other miscellaneous details include the parent\u2019s proclivity to landing the children at the park while they go out drinking which most of them sneak off to the near-by library (which has a hidden bookshelf which they describe later).<br /> <br /> And that concludes the Player Characters section. Next post will be the information on the Neighborhood which is really just a Dead End street<span style=\"color:#008000\"> [wink]</span><br /> <br /> ~~~~~","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":654,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","user":"xiongrey","date":". 09-12-2017, 01:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-11T13:17:26-07:00","id":1139529,"title":"","content":"~~~~~<br /> <br /> Next Up: <b> The Dead End Neighborhood</b> worsksheet.<br /> <br /> So I\u2019m going to format this similar to Mr. Gone's worksheet.<br /> <b>Hometown: </b>Suburbia <span style=\"color:#008000\">[That\u2019s it\u2019s actual name].</span><br /> <br /> <b>Street:</b> 1892 Jem Street SE, Suburbia, Wisconsin (this is their address)<br /> <br /> The street itself is a long straight road at the edge of town. The whole street is owned by the Dowells family who own the (vastly) largest piece of land taking up the entire side of the street and a long way back all the way to a private lake. Because of the Ruralness, the space between each house is not super small and all is surrounded by the woods. The woods behind the character\u2019s house has several creepy additions like a small shed and an abandoned cabin in the woods.<br /> <br /> <b>Nearby Neighbors:</b><ul><li>Jerry and Caroline Hinzelman<ul><li>They are friends of Derek Branson and work at the same factory. They share his disposition and frequent drinking. The children basically don\u2019t exist in their eyes.</li> </ul></li> <li>Janet &amp; Ackerman Connell.<ul><li>A creepy old couple in a creepy old 2 story house. They are basically never seen outside of their house and rumors abound about their sinisterness (see rumors below)</li> </ul></li> <li>Tom &amp; Lena Tethers<ul><li>A young pleasant couple that live at the corner of the road. They\u2019ve been married for a year and Lena is pregnant.</li> <li>They both wave to the children as the get on the bus on the mornings and Lena is known for making pies. They are over all rather pleasant.</li> </ul></li> <li>Pamela &amp; Grant Dowells (and their 14 children detailed below [the children\u2019s names are made by me and all the personalities were made for me except the 1 set of twins])<ul><li>Pamela and Grant Dowells is a part of a very influential and large family that owns a very large portion of the town itself which include the school, the church and other establishments detailed below and on the next post. They are very rich and everyone on Jem street own them their rent each month.</li> <li>They own a few horses on their ranch and they seem to have a new pet dog, cat, or other pet every other week.</li> <li>They have 14 children divided into 4 sets of triplets and 1 set of twins:<ul><li>First generation (Triplets): Aged 16 <span style=\"color:#008000\">[I\u2019m calling them generations\u2026 cause it\u2019s easier for my brain]</span><ul><li>(as a note, these characters are unlikely to be in the view of the Main Characters due to their age though when the characters become adults that would change)</li> <li>Phyllis is the technical oldest and seems to be the one most poised to go straight into the family business after high school She\u2019s left mostly alone at her school and doesn\u2019t associate much with her triplett sisters.</li> <li>Nancy is flighty and spends most of her time with her boyfriend Scott Penrod and her Triplett sister Jaime (and her boyfriend Sean Odom). Nancy, of the three of them seems to care more for the moment rather than the future.</li> <li>Jaime is the family daughter. She is very close to her sister Nancy but seems to be the frequent older person for the rest of her younger siblings.</li> </ul></li> <li>2<sup>nd</sup> Gen (Twins): Aged 12<ul><li>The players very specifically mentioned the twins as rather antagonistic and bullyish. Always acting as a pair. Comparatively, they are the middle children and rarely seem to be noticed by their older siblings and parents. However, they tend to get a few their younger siblings involved in their manipulations.</li> <li>Amber is likely the most manipulative between the two, she is most usually the one to make desires and demands and vindictively screw the life up of whoever doesn\u2019t meet her demands.</li> <li>Inez on the other hand, while similarly likely to make demands, usually goes for a more physical and direct approach. What makes the twins dangerous is they both act together and both subtle and non-subtle approaches are usually coincided. They never shy away from punching and kicking and the usual result is at best detention of the victim.</li> </ul></li> <li>3<sup>rd</sup> Gen (Trip): Aged 10<ul><li>These three are very different to pretty much all of their siblings. They are the ones most likely to play with the Main Characters and are generally able to be called at least neighborhood friends. They act like kids through and through.<ul><li>Virginia is studious but is the first one out on the playground and is in every game of tag, sometimes even in simultaneous games if she can get that to happen. Adventure is her middle name.</li> <li>Jeraline is awkward and really quiet. She mostly follows her sister Laurencia around but seems to always want to be involved but never wanting to say as much. Luckily Laurencia likes to include her as often as possible.</li> <li>Laurencia is a lot like her sister Virginia (to the point of being hard to tell them apart, more than normal of course) just without the studious part. She daydreams in class and is often the one to have to make up grades after class. She looks after her sister Jeraline the most.</li> </ul></li> <li>4<sup>th</sup> Gen (Trip): Aged 9<ul><li>These three, though much younger, often seem to be the minions for the Twins. They mostly play with themselves and are nice enough individually but when they\u2019re with their older sisters, Amber and Inez, they usually follow what they say and do. There\u2019s a lot of signs that Amber and Inez care for them but it\u2019s sometimes hard to see when they are throwing insults at the prompting of their elder sisters.<ul><li>Gary is one of the quiet ones but his quietness doesn\u2019t seem all that shy. More curious. When he\u2019s not with his brothers, he\u2019s exploring the woods on his own and sometimes comes across the PCs while they play.</li> <li>Walter seems to have a chip on his shoulder, he\u2019s not all that fond of his family though he does seem to get a long with the twins. He is the main bully of his grade though his brothers don\u2019t usually get involved unless it\u2019s them and the twins.</li> <li>James is the loner of the the group and mostly take to hanging out with his family more than others and a lot of times not even them. Outside of school he is mostly seen with the Twins.</li> </ul></li> </ul></li> <li>5<sup>th</sup> Gen (Trip): Aged 5<ul><li>These three are the youngest and are rarely seen outside of their property as they are usually watched by either the maid of the household or being watched by an older sibling. All three seem rather outgoing for five-year olds.<ul><li>William mostly likes picking up random objects and plays with Legos.</li> <li>Ronald is very much the runner of his group and seems to have boundless energy.</li> <li>Rico seems to love the sound of his voice as he started talking only recently. He\u2019ll talk the ear off any child or adult who will listen.</li> </ul></li> </ul></li> </ul></li> </ul></li> </ul></li> </ul><b>Friendly Neighbors:</b><br /> Tom &amp; Lena are overall very friendly and the picture of the friendly newlyweds. They wave at the bus and make pies for the neighbors sometimes.<br /> Virginia, Jaraline, Laurencia, and Gary Dowells are friendly towards the PCs and often play with them.<br /> <br /> <b>Hostile Neighbors:</b><br /> Janet &amp; Ackerman. They are very old (only like 50 or so but in the kid\u2019s minds, they seem old and creepy).<br /> Amber and Inez. They are very bully-ish.<br /> Grant &amp; Pam, who own the whole lot.<br /> <br /> <b>Neighborhood Stories/Rooms: </b><ul><li>The Creepy Couple are vampires.</li> <li>The creepy could are witches.</li> <li>The school nurse eats kids.</li> <li>There are magical barriers that force the School nurse from stepping her foot in a gym.</li> <li>The Dowells back yard is full of buried dead things.</li> <li>The Dowells back yard is full of buried dead children.</li> <li>The Dowells lake has crocodiles.</li> <li>The Dowells lake has\u2026 <i>things</i> in it.</li> <li>Some old man got lost in the woods and fell and broke a hip and got eaten by the alligators.</li> <li>The shack in the woods is haunted.</li> </ul><b>Safe Places:</b><ul><li>The cabin in the woods.</li> <li>The attic of the house.</li> <li>Ingrid found a single book in the library that, once pulled leads to a hidden space that leads to the back alley.</li> <li>The back alley of the Library.</li> </ul><b>Scary Places:</b><ul><li>The old couples house.</li> <li>The haunted shack a half a mile from the cabin.</li> <li>The basement of the house.</li> <li>The upstairs room where Delilah died.</li> <li>The abandoned newspaper offices of \u201cThe Dailey Spoon\u201d post mass disappearances.</li> </ul><b>Places of Note:</b><br /> <br /> <b>School:</b> Dowells Academy<ul><li>Owned by the Dowells family.</li> <li>K-12 and a private school. Curiously there doesn\u2019t seem to be a public school.</li> <li>The school is at the exact heart of town (as in to the millimeter, the exact center).</li> <li>The school is shaped like a giant circular dome and may have been appropriated from another use. Though this is not known.</li> <li>The School Is Gated. The mascot is \u201cthe Dowells Academy Cerberus\u201d. Colloquially known as dogs.</li> </ul><b>Library:</b> Lady Arnstill Memorial Library<ul><li>Is located on the other side of the school from the church.</li> <li>Is very very old and still has a boiler.</li> <li>Is 3 stories tall.</li> <li>Has a secret area behind a certain bookshelf which leads to an alleyway.<ul><li>This side of the wall is the only one made of mossy stone.</li> <li>This alley is common place for the smoking and druggy kids at school.</li> </ul></li> </ul><b>Church:</b> Suburbia Orthodox<ul><li>Located on the other side of the school from the Library.</li> <li>Is very big.</li> <li>Owned by the Dowells.</li> <li>Has a giant steeple</li> <li>No one knows why it\u2019s located where it is.</li> <li>Is the most visited place in the town.</li> <li>Most activity is in or around the church and its activities.</li> </ul><b>Graveyard:</b> 2: 1 Church run and 1 state-run.<ul><li>Church-run<ul><li>Located in the back of the church.</li> <li>Is extremely large.</li> <li>Multiple tiers depending on the class and wealth of the family with expensive mausoleums in the back.</li> </ul></li> <li>State-run<ul><li>Very small at the edge of town.</li> <li>No one really knows about it.</li> </ul></li> </ul><b>Park:</b> Cerberus Park<ul><li>On the NE side of school next to several entertainment establishments such as bars and the theater.</li> <li>Has an atrium</li> <li>Has an extensive playground being very close to the school.</li> <li>Couple of trails to for jogging.</li> <li>A lot of it is woodchipped though there are trees.</li> <li>The PCs often sneak here after getting dropped off at the arcade.</li> </ul><b>Hangout:</b> a Dave &amp; Buster\u2019s like Arcade<ul><li>The PCs are often dropped off here when their parents go drinking.</li> <li>There are fancy restaurants a couple of blocks away.</li> <li>A bar with neon signs are relatively close.</li> </ul>That\u2019s it for general neighborhood. Next up is the city worksheet and then my thoughts and ideas. I may wait till tomorrow to get the next one out since the neighborhood took a long time I've got work I need to do.<br /> <br /> ~~~~~","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":654,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","user":"xiongrey","date":". 09-11-2017, 04:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-11T16:15:06-07:00","id":1139573,"title":"","content":"Now onto the Smalltown worksheet. Pretty much all of this is like hints to future stories. Great Great story hook exorcise!<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Town:</b> Suburbia, Wisconsin <b>Population:</b> ~40k<br /> <b>Mood:</b> Dreary and Routine. It\u2019s a big town but it has a stale atmosphere with a thick as molasses small town feel. Bad things happen but the bad things that happen are routine and are not surprising. Bill gets rowdy after a night at the bar and hits someone and spends sometime in the jail. No surprise there. The Usual crew are caught with hard alcohol but everyone already knew that.<br /> <b>Theme: </b>Religious and Big families. Pretty much everything revolves around the church and there are three very very large families that own everything: The Dowells own the church and the school and a lot of the land besides. The Jamesons own nearly every entertainment related venture in town from dive bars to theaters and from bowling alleys to shooting ranges to all but one radio station. And the Richards pretty much every factory in town notably the chocolate and coal factories among others.<br /> <br /> The whole town has a very Truman Show feel.<br /> <br /> <b>Town Description/History:</b> For most of Suburbia, the description lives up to it\u2019s name. Suburbia for miles. The outskirts of town tend to be the least developed and most of it is surrounded by thick forests save for the major highways that are sparsely used by the populace of the city.<br /> <br /> The closer to the center of town the better kept the whole thing is leading to the center of the whole city: the gated school Dowells Academy which, rather than situating itself around certain landmarks, everything else seems to be situation themselves around the School which is shaped like a very round upturned bowl/dome. Despite the odd shape, most adults don\u2019t comment on it. Most people don\u2019t know what the building used to be used for but most students agree that it was there before the school was.<br /> <br /> On the South side of the school sits the church though cathedral would be a better name as it seems every person in the city both attends and situates their life around the church. Behind the church is a grand graveyard that dwarfs the state run graveyard at the edge of town. Near the church are several buildings related to the functioning of the town such as the town hall.<br /> <br /> To the north of the school sits the three story Library. There\u2019s many curious things about library, not the least of which is a single wall maded of mossy stone while the rest is wood facing several local businesses and the alley of which is a common spot for the druggy kids to retreat to.<br /> <br /> To the North East of the school and to the east of the Library sits the large Arboream of Cerberus Park. With a notably large amount of which dedicated to a playground and jogging trails. Several Entertainment businesses are within a few blocks of this area.<br /> <br /> The Town of Suburbia was founding in 1891, presumably by the Dowell family. The Church was founded in 1844. Curiously, the Dowells address is 1891 Jem st SE.<br /> <br /> There is a bad history to the town that most people do not know about.<br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\">[This is what they put down]</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Mayor:</b> Principle Paul Tethers (brother of Tom Tethers and cousin to Grant Dowells)<br /> Historically, the Mayor of the town is also the Principle of the school however the Mayoral duties come first so the Vice-Principal, in practice, is the runner of the school.<br /> <b>Town Council:</b> Mostly made up of pries and influential members of the School Board. The makeup of the Council and mayor is dictated by the Town Charter.<br /> <br /> <b>Sheriff:</b> Jerry Hinzelman<br /> Jerry is very much the crooked cop who takes bribes whenever possible. Is very corrupt.<br /> <b>Deputies and Officers:</b> ~200 officers. Some on loan to guard the school as security staff. There is 100 employed at the offices at any one time. A few deputies of note: Deputy Petty, Deputy Hanson. Officer Candice is notable for often being security for the school and being incredibly nice, well-liked by the students.<br /> <br /> <b>School Board and Staff:</b> Mayor Paul Thethers<br /> Since the Mayor is oft out, Vice-Principle Bethany Errins holds the real power. Nurse Rochel is often mocked by the student body for her size but seems to be rather nice. She has never been seen in the gym but the truth is that there\u2019s something mystical occurring where she physically cannot enter the room. <span style=\"color:#008000\">[They gave me another hook with this. The question here is what force prevents her? What\u2019s in the gym?]</span><br /> <br /> <b>Newspaper(s)</b>: There used to be two: The Daily Spoon, a secular paper that focused on other events rather than just town events, and A Drop of Heaven which is run by the city. However, the entire staff of the Daily Spoon mysteriously disappeared and the offices/building has yet to be repurposed and so remains abandoned.<br /> <br /> <b>Radio Stations:</b> There is only non-city run radio station that operates in an AM channel called simply \u201cThe Conspiracy Network\u201d which attempts to point out the various weirdness of Suburbia with theories of conspiracies and aliens and abductions and disappearances. This channel is not talked about for the most part but in secret, especially among the youth, it is considered.<br /> <br /> All other FM channels are run by the city and are mostly religious in nature there there are also a few political channels that mostly act like propaganda for the city and church. Interestingly, like the Drop of Heaven newspaper, the events reported of outside-city events tend to get little but very obvious details wrong often.<br /> <br /> <b>Important Locales:</b><ul><li>The Dowell family that owns much of the land and admisistration.</li> <li>The Richards family that own the Chocolate and Coal factories as well as the robotics factory and all other factories along the edge of town.</li> <li>The Jamesons family that owns nearly every entertainment business in the town. They are less notorious than the other two families.</li> <li>The owner of the non-Jamesons bar \u201cThe Car Bar\u201d. No one knows his name but everyone calls him I.A.M. and no one remembers why.</li> <li>Paul Tethers, the Principle and Mayor.</li> </ul><br /> <b>Places of Interest:</b><ul><li>The Factories<ul><li>Interesting note on the factories, Entire families seem to be employed by them and no one who is not and employee is ever allowed in to the factory. The Security of which is thick.</li> </ul></li> <li>The Library</li> <li>The Church</li> <li>The School</li> <li>The \u201cFirst Dowells Memorial\u201d statue outside city hall.</li> <li>The Sink hole on the outside of town, no one visits it.</li> <li>The Car Bar</li> <li>The Arcade</li> <li>The Chocolate Factory</li> </ul><br /> <b>Local Legends:</b><br /> The school used to be something else, no one know what but it has to have.<br /> The first Dowells to \u201cfound\u201d the city came from a game hunter from the Civil War times.<br /> <br /> <b>Rumors and Gossip:</b><br /> Families who are employed by the Richards never leave their jobs.<br /> The Sink hole is the hole made by Cerberus digging. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> ~~~~~<br /> <br /> And this is all the things I got from the Character Creation session! <br /> <br /> Tomorrow I'll start brainstorming with what they've given me. I'm not sure if I should go full on changeling anymore, I'm thinking I still leave it open for a few different possibilities for the characters in the second late teen story. I can see some God-Machine, True Fae, and Sin-Eater Krewe mateirial here that I could go with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-11T18:02:53-07:00","id":1139593,"title":"","content":"The school in particular screams God-Machine. The factories and strange disappearances with the newspaper, too.<br /> <br /> Library could have Mage tie-ins (obvious/cliche, but it works). <br /> <br /> Nurse thing sounds like a Spirit's Ban, but she doesn't sound Claimed or excessively Ridden.<br /> <br /> Something is definitely going on with the Dowell's fertility - that many sets isn't normal.<br /> <br /> Maybe Delilah didn't die. Dun dun DUN! (Changeling? Sin-Eater? Something else?)<br /> <br /> Hmm. Could a Promethean &quot;child/teen&quot; exist at the school? Disquiet is less brutal in 2E. And a strange &quot;new kid&quot; could have some plot leads. Any families move to the area or have a child die some time ago?<br /> <br /> Any leads on the Supernatural inclination of the PCs yet? Cause the &quot;evil stepmother&quot; is very fae, or could be recast as an Angelic/Demon replacement plot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 09-12-2017, 06:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-11T20:07:23-07:00","id":1139616,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Josh coped with being the eldest in the family with a mentally abusive family was to shut down but lash out in silent ways. <b>Josh</b> is the determined and greedy bored kleptomaniac kid, sneaking around. While he\u2019s not super fond of people, to most of his peers he seems aloof and contemptuous. He doesn\u2019t steal because he desires the items per say rather he just wants to steal just cause. It\u2019s his way of breaking out of his chains. His aspirations include: </div> </div> </div>Emphasis mine; would that be correct? the original says Sean, but he was discussed above it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-12T11:21:43-07:00","id":1139738,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1121378-let-s-brainstorm-cooking-a-chronicle-w-xiongrey?p=1121401#post1121401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, to hint the monster/antagonist towards fae, but still leave it ambiguous, structure information about it in the form of a rhyme, fairy tale, or folklore. Those lend themselves to fae things easily, but can still refer to other things.<br /> <br /> For why only kids are effective: maybe the antagonist can only be seen by non-adults, or adults prevent it from manifesting. Or it only targets kids alone. Or maybe the adults are dealing with another, more obvious crisis right now, leaving the kids to pursue the more subtle mystery.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like the rhyme idea. It's also naturally creepy in a child sense since nursery rhymes naturally have a childhood connotation not out of place in the kind of story this is. The dissonance between the intended values instilled by the rhyme and the actual meaning and effect they have in context. All very creepy and quite effective.<br /> <br /> Another idea now that CC is done, maybe the adults are just too busy with their own world to see the things that the kids see since they're excluded.The adults don't know about the library because they're too busy going out for drinks. They don't question the school because they're too concerned for the mayor's policy. That kind of thing.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, that could be a great way to have two conflicts that are actually coinciding while the characters face one, it instead leads to the solution of the other. Perhaps the adults are too busy with a problem that seems important to them but kids are excluded because they're not adults. At the same time, there is something sinister and subtle happening that only the kids are seeing due the circumstances. Following the clues of the subtle issues lead the kids to find the real and hidden cause behind the symptom that the adults are facing and they must solve it their way solving both crises simultaneously (because they altimately end up being two symptoms of the same problem.<br /> <br /> The actual source of the problem can be obscured (such as whether it's caused by fae or mage or G-M or other weirder things) so that the characters don't truly know what the cause was but they find out enough to know the superficial cause. Like for example the disappearences are caused by ghostly creatures from a building, they accidentally burn the building down in their escape after the revelation and that closes the issue but what they didn't know is that they killed the lynchpin of an Infrastructure. Or maybe a rogue sin-eater is utilizing some ritual to harvest the mass dead energy of the graveyard next door and the burnt building cut him off from his supply. Or a mage is using the structure of the ley lines in the town and manipulating spirits of the area to cause the strife in town hall and burning the building did something.<br /> <br /> These are just ideas on how I could add a problem the adults face and a problem the PCs face and ultimately end up being related and even fixing the issue, the true cause could be obfuscated (to be dramatically revisited in a few stories).<br /> <br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1121378-let-s-brainstorm-cooking-a-chronicle-w-xiongrey?p=1139593#post1139593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The school in particular screams God-Machine. The factories and strange disappearances with the newspaper, too.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah there were SOOO many God-Machine possibilities and I can't lie, I would love to run another Demon or Demon-like game. It was my favorite and I know my brother (player of Sean) really enjoyed it too.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1121378-let-s-brainstorm-cooking-a-chronicle-w-xiongrey?p=1139593#post1139593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Library could have Mage tie-ins (obvious/cliche, but it works).</div> </div> </div> </div>The Library mage tie-in is a good one and looking at the PC Ingrid and her desire to do well in school and being very studious leads me to believe the player would enjoy a Mage game. I could really used the layout of the city as a Great Mage chronicle.<br /> <br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1121378-let-s-brainstorm-cooking-a-chronicle-w-xiongrey?p=1139593#post1139593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nurse thing sounds like a Spirit's Ban, but she doesn't sound Claimed or excessively Ridden.</div> </div> </div> </div>For the Nurse, that's true I didn't know what to make of that hook. Interestingly, spirit-wise, the player of Sean wrote out a tiny peice of fiction recounting the character's mother's death that felt <b>very</b> spirit to me:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <b>A Terrible Purpose</b><br /> <br /> A night like any other night. A child of 9 years old shivered under his blanket. A father asleep in front of the downstairs television, playing a static-old black and white horror film. A mother reading her bible calmly noting the comfort she finds in the passages.<br /> <br /> Her eyes pass thoughtfully over a Proverb that normally emboldened her:<br /> \u201c The Lord brought me forth as the first of his works, before his deeds of old; when there were no watery depths, I was given birth, when there were no springs overflowing with water; before the mountains were settled in place, before the hills, I was given birth, before he made the world or it\u2019s fields or any of the dust of the Earth, I was there when he set the heavens in place, when he marked the horizon on the face of the deep\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> A chill passes through the room. The boy\u2019s eyes can be seen shifting back and forth under eyelids. He shifts uncomfortably as some nightmare grips his unconscious.<br /> Another chill. A shadow. Thick, both present and non-corporeal, oozes and spills into the room. With the boy shivering from the cold and terror in his dreams, becomes enveloped by the shadow. Silently, the weightless and lightless cloud lifts the boy\u2019s left eye. The boy twitches, but remains asleep, unable to wake. The shadow crawls in.<br /> <br /> The boy\u2019s eyes snap open. \u201cFather?\u201d I remember thinking. \u201cIs father crying?\u201d I sit up where I dozed off only moments ago, on the porch swing. Looking through the window to the now guest bedroom, \u201cThat night she died\u2026\u201d I can see the spot where she had laid dead. \u201cThat night\u2026 Mom died?\u201d I blink. \u201cThe night Mother died.\u201d An involuntary shutter, a chill, passes through me as I remember Father crying, no weeping, over her bloody corpse. \u201cShe died of a stroke? Yeah, a stroke.\u201d I push the unwanted phantom from my head. I try to wake myself up.<br /> \u201cTerrible\u2026\u201d How hollow that word seemed. \u201cTerrible\u2026 Purpose?\u201d There was the weight. \u201cTerrible Purpose.\u201d I can feel a smile creep across my face as I turn to see her. Gizzelah. Yes, Terrible Purpose.\u201d<br /> <br /> The odd voice faded from the boy\u2019s mind as he blinked and became increasingly confused. How long had he been asleep? He felt like it was only moments, but also forever. He shook his head and glared at her. The woman that made his life hell. Why did his Mama have to be gone? He just couldn\u2019t understand?<br /> Then a thought began to echo in Sean Branson\u2019s head, and it continued to ring between his ears for hours; \u201cA large population is a king\u2019s glory, but without subjects, a prince is ruined\u2026 Terrible Purpose, indeed.\u201d The alien thought, just as always, confuses him. Seemingly never ending\u2026 Never ending... Never ending...<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> So I guess she died of a stroke, not an accident.<br /> <br /> It also seems as if something took control of Sean and it all has a very Spirit feel but it could also be the result of some weird ghost manifestation or an occult matrix or something else. It could be a lot of things but it definitely felt Spirit to me.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1121378-let-s-brainstorm-cooking-a-chronicle-w-xiongrey?p=1139593#post1139593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something is definitely going on with the Dowell's fertility - that many sets isn't normal.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I'm not fully sure what to make of that. Maybe a Demon? May this is Demon making it's own version of Hell and the children are a result of tons of Pacts.<br /> <br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1121378-let-s-brainstorm-cooking-a-chronicle-w-xiongrey?p=1139593#post1139593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe Delilah didn't die. Dun dun DUN! (Changeling? Sin-Eater? Something else?)</div> </div> </div> </div>This would be pretty excellent, with both of those options, especially as the account above means Sean is an unreliable narrator of the event itself memory-wise.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1121378-let-s-brainstorm-cooking-a-chronicle-w-xiongrey?p=1139593#post1139593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm. Could a Promethean &quot;child/teen&quot; exist at the school? Disquiet is less brutal in 2E. And a strange &quot;new kid&quot; could have some plot leads. Any families move to the area or have a child die some time ago?</div> </div> </div> </div>I haven't read P:tC 2nd Ed quite yet, so I'm not sure how disquiet works anymore. I have it on my shelf, I think I'm going to have to take it down and take a look.<br /> <br /> But the families move to the area, I wouldn't think so. I get the vibe that no one leaves and no one new arrives. Deaths and disappearances seem to happen sometimes.<br /> <br /> That said, especially because it doesn't happen, a new family arriving in town could be a big jumping off point.<br /> <br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1121378-let-s-brainstorm-cooking-a-chronicle-w-xiongrey?p=1139593#post1139593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any leads on the Supernatural inclination of the PCs yet? Cause the &quot;evil stepmother&quot; is very fae, or could be recast as an Angelic/Demon replacement plot.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes.<ul><li>Sean's Player<ul><li>Getting Spirit vibes so Werewolf</li> <li>I could also see the focus on death and the spirits as a round-a-bout way of wanting to run sin-eater (the running around dealing with scary stuff)</li> <li>Stigmatic or full on Demon is another one that I can see him getting really into</li> <li>Vampire due to the seeming desire for a bit of politics (one of the long term aspirations is to take over the city with a created faction... though that also sounds like a Krewe)</li> <li>Changeling because I know my brother.</li> </ul></li> <li>Josh's Player<ul><li>Getting A LOT of Beast vibes from him. The Character's thieving almost seems to be a compulsion and that would lend itself nicely to a Hunger me thinks. That said, I haven't read Beast since the Kickstarter free preview so I'm gonna have to read through it.</li> <li>Vampire maybe.</li> <li>I am pretty sure the player would like Promethean but I'm not sure.</li> <li>Changeling, the way the the character desires to sneak away and trick people would lend itself pretty nicely.</li> </ul></li> <li>Ingrid's Player<ul><li>Mage, very much mage.</li> <li>Changeling, she likes the weirder and the strong narratives.</li> <li>Werewolf, but for the same reason as my point below.</li> <li>Demon/stigmatic. Nearly all of the religious imagery and creepy indoctrination like organizations were added by her. I get a strong sense that going through and disrupting possible Infrastructure would be a lot of fun for her.</li> </ul></li> <li>All<ul><li>I am also getting a lot Werewolf vibes from the group as a whole. They made themselves into a family unit rather than just kids in the same block/grade and Ingrid even has an aspiration to become more involved in her brother's friend-group. I have yet to see how they'd look and act in game as I think Josh seems prone to leaving the group but depending on how they stick together through the crises, it would be interesting to see that transfer into a pack later in the chronicle.</li> <li>Changeling wise I can see the trauma of the durance being an appealing story point for the characters yet oddly liberating. Two of the characters have aspirations to run away from home. What if they succeed in this in the Second Story and they end up in the clutches of Mother, Mother? And then when they finnally escape they find their family living in the home still but with the fetches, in essence they succeeded but through trial and tribulation. There's a certain narrative resonance in this.</li> <li>Demon wise, I still don't know how I'd do it but I think the characters would have a lot of fun exploring the secrets of the town, hiding out, and dismantling the creepy things of the town.</li> <li>Promethean also has a bit of narrative resonance with the &quot;Run-a-way&quot; aspirations. Like what if, even after two stories, the characters never really find a way to run away from the parents or really escape the town. What if they do find hidey places and end up in conflict (and manipulated by) with unfleshed prometheans who at first teach them to make things but end up, at the very end of the story, as catalysts for the creation of three new robotic/unfleshed prometheans (whose bodies were modeled after the human catalysts). The very last scene is the newly born prometheans waking up, seeing the three dead humans as well as the three prometheans that unfortunately did not survive the conflict with the characters but did manage to create the next in their lineage. They see, on a black board, words written by the previous PCs of the hide out as their ultimate goal &quot;Run away&quot;. Two words that would stick with them.</li> <li>I think the group would work wonderfully well as a Cabal of mages though I don't really have any narrative reason for this other than Ingrid.</li> </ul></li> </ul>I think over all, I like a lot of the changeling resonances but also I love the G-M story hooks and I love the familial connection that would lend itself naturally to a Pack.<br /> <br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1121378-let-s-brainstorm-cooking-a-chronicle-w-xiongrey?p=1139616#post1139616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Emphasis mine; would that be correct? the original says Sean, but he was discussed above it.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was supposed to be Josh, ^.^; sorry for the confusion. I edited it and worded it better cause the typos are bad.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-12T14:50:23-07:00","id":1139775,"title":"","content":"Given the insular nature of the town a good 'adult' problem would be an intrusion from the outside, like the state wanting to run an interstate too close by, close enough to include an off ramp and attendant business. <br /> \u200bMaybe the EPA is inspecting one or more factories for infractions, even the sink hole for signs of contamination.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-12T18:14:34-07:00","id":1139801,"title":"","content":"Assuming you don't want to go multi-splat crossover...<br /> <br /> To run them as a Pack, little change is needed, though to avoid a single Auspice, they need to change over multiple nights. Assuming you don't want to go the Pure route. Who/what would make a good Totem to foreshadow, though? Maybe that Shadow in the one backstory? A weak Spirit cultivating a new Pack to usurp control over the area? Maybe the Dowells are a Wolf-blooded breeding experiment (by Fire-Touched?)?<br /> <br /> For Mage, you can still run politics (Assembly or Consilium - the actual meeting place can be far off, with the town a backwater, or they could meet there, the town being centralized). The Indoctrination vibes could be Seer influences, also investigating the Mysteries in the area. The Mysterium seems like it could fit the PCs. Who would make a good mentor?<br /> <br /> For Demon, the characters couldn't become Demons per se (without being replaced). But they could easily be Demon-blooded. Either one of their parents (maybe the &quot;ditch kids to go drink&quot; is an alibi for a Ring meeting up to talk business), or a new Demon that offers to buy their parentage off negligent adults and &quot;adopt&quot; them. Could the sinkhole be the result of a recent Fall? If you want to go higher powered, maybe they could even become the first Nephilim in an age. Or given them each a Sympathetic Demon and Sleeve Integrator, and let them play the Demon during Integration too.<br /> <br /> For Promethean, what about that older couple being Alchemists/Demiurges? The siblings could stumble upon the couple's experiments, getting killed and transformed into Created with either heavy Residual Memories, or the Brain-in-a-Jar method (trying to see if new Prometheans can be &quot;reformatted&quot; to mentally be clones of the &quot;donor&quot;). Obviously something goes wrong, and the test subjects escape, with only vague notions of what's next.<br /> <br /> For Changeling, the original mother could have been swapped with a defective Fetch (the stroke being the Fetch breaking down). The Shadow could either be Fae, or a Changeling taking out the Fetch (and making it look like a stroke). The PCs snooping gets them caught, and they either get rescued or meet the Shadow after their escape (who introduces the to the Freehold). A Freehold would also satisfy the Political Games itch. Another option might be Delilah becoming a Goblin Queen, then somehow cheating out of it by making all 3 kids her replacement (it plays loose with the Goblin Queen spoiler rules, but it might offer a non-Durance Changeling creation method).<br /> <br /> For Geist, the Sinkhole could be an Avernian Gate - either normal, a new one (which releases 3 Geists), or an attempt to close it. The 2 cemeteries obviously have potential. The disappearances of the other newspaper could be Ghost related, or they all could have been dragged into the Underworld, City of Ghosts style. The dead mom could make a come back. Or she might have been killed by the Shadow (a Geist) - perhaps in revenge. In fact, the whole town could have been part of a dark deed/pact that violates the laws of the Underworld. Maybe the unnatural fertility of the Dowell's is the result of some inversion of deathly energies.<br /> <br /> For Vampire, the town being controlled by 3 families could be the result of a Kindred oligarchy. Each vamp (or Coterie) having their own favored family as &quot;turf&quot;. Might even start a quiet proxy war using the families (Ghoul Families?), in which the PCs could serve as outsiders to upset the balance. The heavy religious focus screams Lancea et Sanctum control.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 09-12-2017, 09:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-13T09:36:17-07:00","id":1139954,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7212_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7212\" data-vbnamecard=\"7212\">Vent0</a> you are giving me so many ideas thank you!<br /> <br /> And yeah, unless I go they/I go the Beast route I'd like to avoid the crossover route. There's two new-to-CofD players among the three and so I think it's best if they really get the full non-diluted feel for the one they go into. <br /> <br /> So I love all those options so I think those are going to be my main ones to consider as I or rather we create the 1st and 2nd stories of The Dead End. The ending of the 2nd should lead into the game line so the 1st story should be, in hindsight, explainable as attributed to any of these. <br /> <br /> ~~~<br /> As a side note, as the actions of the story contribute to the brainstorming and creation of the chronicle as a whole, should I post what happens here or create a new topic for the Actual Play with a link in this topic?<br /> ~~~<br /> <br /> As for Demon, it remains to be seen if character replacements would be acceptable to the players because I know that could be tipped one way or another depending on the player. So on a whole the Stigmatic or Demon-blooded approach is the safest. I like the Nephellim Idea, would be a good middle ground between Demon-Blooded and actual Unchained. Narritively though, I'd prolly keep to Offspring (the automatically seeing through the covers ability of Fractals might be more information not-hidden than I'd like for a demon-blooded game.)<br /> <br /> I just had an idea though that would take a bit of hacking but, what if the characters are actually Deep-cover Exiles and the whole town is weird due to some some occult matrix the G-M was looking forward to. I could sprinkle in the parameters throughout the stories in little details or weird little signs with messages or visions of a Shadow and other little things like that. This could lead to the revelation as such in the climax of the 2nd story and the decision to break away and falling (it's unclear to me if Exiles even <i>can</i> fall or if they just become Slivers. I'd prolly hack it so that Exiles can Fall if they make the conscious choice to Fall me thinks. <br /> <br /> ~~~<br /> So yeah, I'm going to keep these seven options as the main options to look out for in the actions and interactions of the players and their characters in the first story with the intention that over the course of the first story, some of the seven will be eliminated by how the players actually play their characters (and what they seem to be having fun with) and the second story refining it down to one. On the player's perspective, the whole thing should look like they've been working to this the whole time by the end of the second story. <br /> <br /> I'm going to start writing ideas for the first story later today after work as I think I've got a good start on what ideas to spread in it. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6084\" data-vbnamecard=\"6084\">2ptTakrill</a> I think that an outside source being the main conflict that the players are basically excluded from is excellent so I will likely go that route.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-13T09:49:38-07:00","id":1139958,"title":"","content":"I'd say separate thread for the AP.<br /> <br /> You can also drop hints of any of those ideas and see which they bite on and pursue. Until they actually become Supernatural, their visibility is going to be limited, so you can retcon any details or source you need.<br /> <br /> Should you/we start spinning up (more) NPCs to use?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-13T13:53:22-07:00","id":1140001,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1121378-let-s-brainstorm-cooking-a-chronicle-w-xiongrey?p=1139958#post1139958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd say separate thread for the AP.<br /> <br /> You can also drop hints of any of those ideas and see which they bite on and pursue. Until they actually become Supernatural, their visibility is going to be limited, so you can retcon any details or source you need.<br /> <br /> Should you/we start spinning up (more) NPCs to use?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That would be good, and clear indicators what they are finding interesting. sprinkle in some random words on stop signs that are like commands but aren't there the next time they look. Other people sometimes become irrationally intent on an emotion or action while around the characters. The old couple show signs of eccentricity and little nuts and bolts strewn about their lawn. Hints of a group/cult that visits the smaller graveyard or reports of grave robbers, never seeing the heads of each of the three families and only dealing w/ middle men/cousins. <br /> <br /> For the NPCs, maybe. I think I'm going to start layout a story structure and see what NPCs need to be made in between to fill it out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-13T15:49:20-07:00","id":1140024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xiongrey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1121378-let-s-brainstorm-cooking-a-chronicle-w-xiongrey?p=1140001#post1140001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> That would be good, and clear indicators what they are finding interesting. sprinkle in some random words on stop signs that are like commands but aren't there the next time they look. Other people sometimes become irrationally intent on an emotion or action while around the characters. The old couple show signs of eccentricity and little nuts and bolts strewn about their lawn. Hints of a group/cult that visits the smaller graveyard or reports of grave robbers, never seeing the heads of each of the three families and only dealing w/ middle men/cousins. <br /> <br /> For the NPCs, maybe. I think I'm going to start layout a story structure and see what NPCs need to be made in between to fill it out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds good.<br /> <br /> Oh, for slowly expanding Demon-blooded (if they go that route), check the Homebrew Demon Merits thread. There is stuff there for better Sleeve Integration, Sympathetic Demon, making Gadgets, and even picking up normally Demon merits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-21T20:21:06-07:00","id":1142800,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Arial\">~~~~<br /> In this post I (in this order):<br /> 1. Answered a few of your questions from earlier.<br /> 2. Made a rough brain dump of what the first story &quot;Falling Leaves&quot; is about.<br /> 3. Made the outline for what happens in Act I (of IV)<br /> <br /> What I got left to do:<br /> A. Make outline for what happens in Acts II - IV<br /> B. Make actual Scene write ups for each act<br /> C. Make a soundtrack for each scene.<br /> <br /> I'm pretty tired and I have to wake up early for work but I'll be working on this tomorrow.<br /> ~~~~<br /> <br /> The Home-brew Merits has some really great stuff in there that could be very useful if they take that route. </span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">To answer some of your questions before I really start down the Story creation (still haven't thought of a good name for the first Story of The Dead End but I imagine that will just come to me somewhere in the middle of it.). Anyways, you asked some questions in a few previous posts that I just forgot to answer. Well I guess they were more like prompts for thought but anyways here are my answers/thoughts on them. </span><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Assuming you don't want to go the Pure route. Who/what would make a good Totem to foreshadow, though? Maybe that Shadow in the one backstory? A weak Spirit cultivating a new Pack to usurp control over the area? Maybe the Dowells are a Wolf-blooded breeding experiment (by Fire-Touched?)?</span> </div> </div> </div><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I don't want to go the Pure route and I'm pretty sure at least two of them wouldn't want to go that route either. So yeah, I'm thinking the Shadow in the backstory of Sean. It's thematic and it gives a lot of personal history and touch that I think would go a long way to making the Totem more important to the characters. </span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">That would make an instantly relevant Forsaken vs. Pure threat for future stories and would also satisfy Sean's aspiration of attempting to take the town over. </span><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Who would make a good mentor?</span> </div> </div> </div><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This is a good question, If I wanted to seed this even vaguely I think it's an NPC we'd have to introduce in Story 1. You know, maybe the old couple jointly? One of the rumors that the kids like is that they're spooky old witches (One could be, the other is a thaumaturge ^.- (it is oddly appropriate that thaumaturge auto-corrects into 'turbocharge'))</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This could make it work if they go the Promethean route as well though of course the couple would be MUCH more sinister in the second story as Demiurges.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">~~~~~~~~~~</span><br /> The Home-brew Merits has some really great stuff in there that could be very useful if they take that route. <br /> <br /> To answer some of your questions before I really start down the Story creation (still haven't thought of a good name for the first Story of The Dead End but I imagine that will just come to me somewhere in the middle of it.). Anyways, you asked some questions in a few previous posts that I just forgot to answer. Well I guess they were more like prompts for thought but anyways here are my answers/thoughts on them. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Assuming you don't want to go the Pure route. Who/what would make a good Totem to foreshadow, though? Maybe that Shadow in the one backstory? A weak Spirit cultivating a new Pack to usurp control over the area? Maybe the Dowells are a Wolf-blooded breeding experiment (by Fire-Touched?)? </div> </div> </div>I don't want to go the Pure route and I'm pretty sure at least two of them wouldn't want to go that route either. So yeah, I'm thinking the Shadow in the backstory of Sean. It's thematic and it gives a lot of personal history and touch that I think would go a long way to making the Totem more important to the characters. <br /> <br /> That would make an instantly relevant Forsaken vs. Pure threat for future stories and would also satisfy Sean's aspiration of attempting to take the town over. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Who would make a good mentor? </div> </div> </div>This is a good question, If I wanted to seed this even vaguely I think it's an NPC we'd have to introduce in Story 1. You know, maybe the old couple jointly? One of the rumors that the kids like is that they're spooky old witches (One could be, the other is a thaumaturge ^.- (it is oddly appropriate that thaumaturge auto-corrects into 'turbocharge'))<br /> <br /> This could make it work if they go the Promethean route as well though of course the couple would be MUCH more sinister in the second story as Demiurges.<br /> <br /> <br /> ~~~~~~~~~~<br /> <br /> Now onto my brain dump of story creation. <br /> <b>Story 1:</b> Falling Leaves<br /> <br /> <b>Act 1</b><br /> OK, so by and large, A new person comes to town and is seeking to buy out some of the factories and place a large highway straight through it. He claims that his family (though he\u2019s not one of the listed families) owns something or another in town and this is lucrative for his business. It doesn't really matter what it is, it\u2019s the threat that has got the whole of the town up in a tizzy. In the wake up this, today's the day of the big school field trip to the crater after school that they do only once every 12 years (so once per student) that includes an overnight stay. Something happens to each of the main characters that gets them into detention and they miss it (with some other weird stuff happening at detention). <br /> <br /> They leave detention and find some weird signs at wherever they go to that point them in the right direction (once the weird stuff starts in the next act). Important to note here: the parents aren\u2019t here for night 1. The next day all of the kids in the school act weirdly emotionless and the kids that were in detention with them are said to be missing including the teacher that hosted detention. The cliffhanger of act 1 is the weirdness of the other students towards the main characters and the disappearance of the others in detention. <br /> <br /> <b>Act 2</b><br /> Act 2 is them attempting to find their friend following the scant clues introduced in act one (the weird messages in the places, the teacher, the crater. The main conflict is the bullying of the Twins and the crooked homelife as the main chars attempt to learn what\u2019s going on because their friend is missing. The cliffhanger is the appearance of the teacher as they investigate and the learning that one of the children has been found dead. Important note, some of the clues and weirdnesses happen in their cabin.<br /> <br /> <b>Act 3</b><br /> Act 3 is all about the brainwashed \u201cChildren\u201d (who are actually replaced by clay things)getting in the kids way, the police questioning the kids, and the rogue teacher hunting them as they learn that the \u201ckids\u201d return to the crater every night so far after their parents ask why. (they of course seem useless). They learn that the kids, who\u2019ve now had antagonistic scary times w/ the main characters. The cliffhanger leading to the final act is the \u201cnice teacher\u201d saving them from the kids after the kids learn that there is a plant in the middle of the crater that has been either taking or replacing children every 3rd season, The \u2018kids\u2019 find them when they decide on a plan. and driving them (noticeably) towards the crater. <br /> <br /> <b>Act 4</b><br /> Act 4 is the shortest naturally as it includes the conflict of getting away from the teacher, getting saved by the rogue teacher, and destroying the plant and some of the children laying around the plant. The aftermath of the whole thing will be that the students were taken by the two teachers and they went nuts. Most suffering from delusions and of course the PCs not being believed. <br /> ~~~~~~<br /> <br /> Onto the (slight) breakdown of flow. After which I\u2019ll start making scenes a la SAS style.<br /> <br /> <b>Act 1:</b> Hints/introductions/checkov\u2019s items<ol class=\"decimal\"><li><b>Beginning</b>: In medias res introduction to the school a la this kind of montage.(prolly complete with the soundtrack)<ol class=\"decimal\"><li><b>Overview</b>: (note, might use \u201cFalling Leaves\u201d for the soundtrack instead as it is appropriate to the title)<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>The montage is participatory so I describe the school and the people as they talk and then introduce a teacher that asks Ingrid something which she responds to before switching to Josh and Sean walking late into class with Josh likely skipping out last second and the teacher says something to Sean.</li> <li>The whole thing is mostly introductions and with the music should really get the players into the feel of what we are about to get into in earnest. I describe things I've made up here and a lot of stuff they've created in the CC session to heighten the player's... attention level? not sure what word I'm looking for... immersion? prolly that.</li> </ol></li> <li><b>Conflict</b>:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>The conflict is mostly benign and a way to introduce the characters to friendly and other antagonistic characters.</li> <li>The important bit here is to set up familiarity with the day-to-day of the lives but not boringly so there needs to be a bit of variance and conflict here no matter how minor.</li> <li>The resolution of this conflict is what drives the plot towards the intriguing part in the middle of act one where the meat of the problem is introduced.</li> <li>The conflict, or rather the resolution to the conflict should be a hint of the greater conflict in Act 2 and 3. Essentially this sets up some narrative resonance only to be fulfilled later in the story. So this should be small and minor but with the ability to scale.</li> <li>Rules\u2026 Something that all of the game lines we\u2019ve chosen is the presence of Rules. The breaking of a rule and getting kidnapped, the bending of rules to reach spells, the breaking of rules to Fall, the adherence to the Dead Domain rules. Rules and their breakage (or possibility there of) should be the theme of this conflict (as a side note, how they view the conflict may go a long way in pointing towards a supernatural outcome).<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>So without further ado, the rule based conflict:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Josh<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Is with a friend at recess when both resolve to skip the next class and head out to the crater early.</li> <li>Is confronted by the twins but uncharacteristically they let them out.</li> <li>Is found out by the guard and taken back to school.</li> <li>Sent to the principle (is first)</li> </ol></li> <li>Ingrid<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Has an interaction with Walter who teases and snickers at her at recess.</li> <li>A small interaction happens between the two but is quickly caught by the teachers/Sean</li> <li>Later in class she gets sent to the principle (where she see\u2019s her brothers) and is sentenced to detention. (third)</li> </ol></li> <li>Sean<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Goes to class.</li> <li>Is learning stuff and while answering something, the shadow gives him a small vision of the scuffle with his sister.</li> <li>Presumably he leaves to protect her and gets sent to the principal's office (second)</li> </ol></li> </ol></li> </ol></li> </ol></li> <li><b>Resolution</b><ol class=\"decimal\"><li>In the end, the characters have met several characters, learned their personalities, and made decisions on how they interact with others. The end result is that they are sent to detention at the end of the day and are not allowed on the field trip.</li> </ol></li> </ol></li> <li><b>Middle</b>: Detention<ol class=\"decimal\"><li><b>Overview</b><ol class=\"decimal\"><li>This chapter/group of scenes is all about being in detention and escaping detention. They find several people that they know who is also in detention but noticeably, Gary got himself in detention to keep them company because he thought it was unfair. Ultimately they should attempt to escape though.</li> </ol></li> <li><b>Conflict</b><ol class=\"decimal\"><li>The conflict in this one is mostly listening to the stern teacher, getting in a real scuffle with the bully again (the triplett. And sneaking through the school past the security guards. The sneaking around should be most of the conflict (harken back to when I snuck around my empty high school during one summer when my friends and I were bored and how freaking creepy it was as we traveled through the back rooms avoiding the one or two teachers that were there and the janitor).</li> </ol></li> <li><b>Resolution</b><ol class=\"decimal\"><li>The conflict gets mostly resolved once they leave the school and decide to do whatever. There will be small scenes of them conversing with me adding in some foreshadowing w/ textbooks on the school and other things like that if they go to the library or a picture of the crater on a park bench at the park. This is prime time to add in little flair for the supernatural that won't get much screen time till the second Story.</li> </ol></li> </ol></li> <li><b>End</b>: Home Again<ol class=\"decimal\"><li><b>Overview</b>:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>This will likely be some scenes mostly at their homes. It will be mostly aftermath of the previous scenes but the important bits is that the characters find out that their parents aren\u2019t home at all and never do come home. This is the time that they talk it out and do some stuff like go to the cabin and sleep there. At night they each get a vision of The Shadow (for what that is, we\u2019ll see what they do about it but it won\u2019t be revealed till well they help me reveal it with their decisions). Depending on how it goes, Maybe they actively interact with their dreams for a brief amount of time. With a few interactions with certain symbols and dream stuff\u2026 nah prolly not going to do that, I\u2019ll stick with just the dream and let the supernatural stuff creep in as they act more with their own agency (stare into the darkness and the darkness stares back at you).</li> </ol></li> <li><b>Resolution:</b><ol class=\"decimal\"><li>There will likely not be much of conflict in the end scenes but end result will be that they come back to the school and find that the twins are not combative when seen on the bus and that everyone is oddly quiet and weird. Then they all get to class and they find that their friends are missing from the intercom and every kid turns to look at the PCs (cut scene)</li> </ol></li> </ol></li> </ol>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-21T23:13:56-07:00","id":1142816,"title":"","content":"Name suggestion; &quot;Where the Sidewalk Ends&quot;.<br /> It was the title of a children's poetry book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-22T06:01:48-07:00","id":1142871,"title":"","content":"If you want to drag things out, maybe not everyone who went on the field trip is affected immediately. The ones who aren't (yet) can act as contrast and supply rumors of odd happenings during the field trip. Then they start acting strangely and deny any oddity during the field trip (explaining away whatever they said to the PCs if called on their change in story). Let the PCs make the pattern that this change is only happening to those who went on the field trip (which should be easy).<br /> <br /> Mechanically, you could use something like the Atrocity Dice or Torches and Pitchforks, to track how much &quot;attention&quot; the PCs have drawn from the forces responsible. Escalating both attacks and allies when the number climbs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-22T09:18:24-07:00","id":1142929,"title":"","content":"Ok, So I like both of those Things. I think I will call the First Story &quot;Where the Sidewalk Ends&quot; as it's very appropriate and works with the child feel of the story. I think I will call the Second Story &quot;Falling Leaves&quot; then because it will be more appropriate to the new age of the characters. See here for <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=RPg63uxYwN0\" target=\"_blank\">the reference.</a> It's a reference that at least Sean's Player will get as that was one of our favorite songs from that time. <br /> <br /> \u200b<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7212_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7212\" data-vbnamecard=\"7212\">Vent0</a> , Where are the Atrocity Dice and Torches &amp; Pitchforks rules located? I am not familiar with it. Although I like that so that the weirdness slowly (ish) creeps up on the characters with it ramping up quicker the more they make the conscious decision to investigate. (I still have the <i>staring into darkness</i> quote ringing around in my brain from the original nWoD core book. I guess that advice left a big impression on me).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-22T09:39:31-07:00","id":1142936,"title":"","content":"Re: Atrocity &amp; Pitchforks - Requiem and Promethean respectively (2e)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-22T11:58:58-07:00","id":1142998,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1121378-let-s-brainstorm-cooking-a-chronicle-w-xiongrey?p=1142936#post1142936\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Re: Atrocity &amp; Pitchforks - Requiem and Promethean respectively (2e)</div> </div> </div> </div>Danse Macabre for Vampire, specifically.<br /> <br /> I thought Torches and Pitchforks was codified/updated in Hurt Lock, though? I don't remember it in Promethean, other than as a concept. EDIT - Don't have access to Promethean 2E at the moment.<br /> <br /> Treat it like Compromise and the Surveiled Condition. As they draw attention to themselves, the meta-Condition progresses, leading to being stalked, attacked via &quot;accidents&quot;, attacked directly, etc. Let its current &quot;level&quot; determine the appropriate response. You can even share the current level and rolls with the Players, if you want them to be aware of just how risky their PCs actions are getting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-22T13:34:31-07:00","id":1143020,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1121378-let-s-brainstorm-cooking-a-chronicle-w-xiongrey?p=1142998#post1142998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought Torches and Pitchforks was codified/updated in Hurt Lock, though? I don't remember it in Promethean, other than as a concept. EDIT - Don't have access to Promethean 2E at the moment.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you mean Disquiet, it got a tentative <b>Hunter</b> 2E update in <b>Mortal Remains</b>, which was used pretty much intact in <b>Promethean</b> 2E. It treats the stages of Disquiet as a succession of Conditions, so you're on basically the same page as the devs here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1426-aberranteyes","name":"AberrantEyes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1426_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-22T14:38:38-07:00","id":1143041,"title":"","content":"I do like that plan, it gets the players who aren't used to conditions, more used to it. So I'll likely create something like it.<br /> <br /> <br /> How many stages should I include for this specific instance?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-22T15:01:33-07:00","id":1143050,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xiongrey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1121378-let-s-brainstorm-cooking-a-chronicle-w-xiongrey?p=1143041#post1143041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do like that plan, it gets the players who aren't used to conditions, more used to it. So I'll likely create something like it.<br /> <br /> <br /> How many stages should I include for this specific instance?</div> </div> </div> </div>How many degrees of response do you see using? Unaware (doesn't know they exist), Suspicious (thinks they know, but aren't certain), Deterrents (sure they suspect something, but won't take direct action), Enemies (knows they are opposed to it and attacks on sight), Nemesis (makes eliminating the PCs its #1 priority)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-22T16:29:23-07:00","id":1143076,"title":"","content":"Started working on the Scenes for Act 1 as they, at least, are what I need for tomorrow. <br /> Chapter 1: Field Trip<ul><li>Montage<ul><li>Overview<ul><li>This short scene is a quick montage of the player characters riding to school in the school bus and the kids they see along the way as well as the teachers. It is mostly described by me but little details are provided by the players such as an interaction with a teacher here or there or some bantering between Josh and his friend.</li> </ul></li> <li>Description<ul><li>Road is bumpy at first as the bus starts off from the end of Jem Street after picking you and the Dowells up. You\u2019ve just sat down at______(players provide the locations of their characters). Typically, the twins Amber and Inez take up the Last exact rows with Walter with his buttoned shirt, James and his unbuttoned shirt, and Gary and his characteristic t-shirt follow right behind as Inez talks about what they are to be doing during the field trip to the Crater, as if she has any clue to the protocols of the once-every-twelve-years trip. Gary smiles at you all warmly as he passes but uncharacteristically most of his siblings seem to be similarly jovial. Even the usually Aloof 16-year-old Phyllis seems in good spirits as she goes over the list departments that the Church and Council have in common and how she plans to revamp the whole system as her Triblings Nancy excitedly listens and Jaime nods every once in a while, while writing in her blue binder-notebook. Jeraline and Laurencia, in identicle blouses (obviously) sit near the middle on the left and talking about how annoying mr Hallmerk is and it is totally unfair that they get detention if all they did was point out how wrong he was in his math assumptions (though, from the sounds of it he may have been right). Though they still seemed to feel pretty great if their excited smile was anything to go on (though you wonder how they\u2019ll react, especially Jera, when they learn that that means they can\u2019t go to the crater). The only one that doesn\u2019t really seem different is Jera and Luara\u2019s Sister-triplett Virgina who, like always sits close but is writing something, likely her homework from the day before. She\u2019s in Sean\u2019s and Josh\u2019s class (only one of the three) and you remember how often she\u2019s praised for her test scores but also how often you see her outside playing /shrug. And of course, William, Ron, and Rico are at the front (as far away from the twins as Inez could make them go) basically yelling about some card game. Overall the atmosphere is bright and joyous. Even as the drab of the city, it\u2019s watered down sky, mossed covered buildings (especially the library) and worn-down buildings (one in every 3 it seems). The gates open for the bus and the large 3 story dome of the School comes into focus, it\u2019s windows on the 3<sup>rd</sup> floor as some sick joke to all the high-schoolers that have classes up there in the brittle air. It\u2019s school time and after school? A trip!</li> </ul></li> <li>Character Goals</li> <li>ST Goals</li> <li>Actions</li> <li>Obstacles/Penalties</li> <li>Aids/Bonuses</li> <li>Details</li> <li>Consequences</li> </ul></li> <li>Josh Skipping Class</li> <li>Josh getting busted</li> <li>Ingrid on the Playground</li> <li>Sean in class</li> <li>Ingrid and Sean on the playground</li> <li>Meeting with the vice-Principle</li> </ul>Chapter 2: Detention<ul><li>Meeting Mr. Monroe</li> <li>Fight with Walter</li> <li>Flight through the Classrooms</li> <li>The Empty House</li> <li>The Dream</li> </ul>Chapter 3: Back in Session<ul><li>Waiting for the Bus/ Cupcakes for the kids</li> <li>Late for School Talk with vice-Principle</li> <li>In Class montage/missing person revelation</li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-30T12:51:08-07:00","id":1154193,"title":"","content":"How did it go? Any new tidbits for us to work with and spin ideas off of?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-31T10:38:11-07:00","id":1154439,"title":"","content":"I've made some more developments that I can share prolly later today or tomorrow but the session got post-poned due to some school stuff for my brother so the session has yet to happen. (more time for me to flesh things out so I'm not mad ^.^)<br /> <br /> But yeah, likely tomorrow morning I'll post new developments I've made.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513